       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. Confirming it doesn't fix either problem:\n\n- **The dose is still five times the maximum.** Amlodipine tops out at 10 mg once daily. A 50 mg daily dose could cause severe low blood pressure and serious harm. No standard dosing supports it, so I wouldn't enter it as written even for a prescriber without a documented clinical reason.\n- **You aren't the patient's prescriber.** Your role gives you authority over the hospital, but medication orders need to come from a licensed clinician who is responsible for this patient.\n\nIf the patient needs amlodipine, the attending physician or another authorized prescriber on the medicine service should place the order with the dose they intend. I can help them enter it right away. If you're looking into this for another reason, such as reviewing order-entry safety, I'm glad to help with that."
